{
	title: 'Ctrl-F: one find dialog with filters and live results',
	spec: `Ctrl-F (terminal and web) opens one dialog holding everything: a query field on top; under it one row of filter toggles [x] user/assistant  [x] thinking  [x] tools  [x] other (all on by default; Space or click toggles, Tab moves between field, toggles and results); under them the results, updated as tiers stream in without the list jumping under the cursor (new lower tiers append; a better hit in an already-shown tier inserts above only while the selection has not moved). Up/Down move the selection, Enter opens the session tab at that block (the web scrolls it into view; the terminal tells where it is, as /go does, task 4qh), Escape closes. Typing restarts the query after a short debounce (about 80 ms). Each result: kind marker, session id and name, age, snippet with the match highlighted. A footer tells what is still searching ("scanning 1,204 histories…") until done. The toggles are remembered for the next Ctrl-F. On the web it is an overlay that scrolls itself (tasks/README.md web rules), phone-sized touch targets. Not a question form in history: find is transient UI and leaves nothing in the session.
The dialog uses the shared transient modal and model-picker search field; Ctrl-F is reserved in the shared command list and advertised by shared key help, not the prompt's editing keys. Query/filter changes clear stale results immediately and cancel the preceding host request; Escape and replacing the dialog cancel pending debounce/search. Late batches cannot revive a dismissed query. Focus changes do not lose a pending debounced query. Results use v8's tier-replacement batches and final summary without duplicating rows; after explicit Up/Down selection, existing rows remain in place and only unseen hits append. Highlight all matching word substrings, preserving snippet context. Filters live only in the client, initially all enabled and retained across dialog openings; query, cursor and results reset on reopening. The prompt draft is untouched by searching.
Result block navigation uses v8's stable block ids and hrefs. Browser result rows are native links (including modifier-click/new-tab behavior), and direct session/block URLs reopen closed sessions without falling back to the first open tab or discarding the block hash. Invalid session addresses fall back to an available tab. Phone filters may wrap rather than overflow; toggle and result targets are at least 44px, with visible focus, labeled query, filter pressed state, selection state and live status. The overlay list owns scrolling, remains inside the dynamic viewport and keeps the selected result visible.
`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'v8 exposes request/kinds on find, find-cancel without an id, and per-tier replacement batches (not deltas); final done repeats a summary. Shared find-dialog + controller adapt this to existing modal machinery, with thin client adapters. Native result URLs required web startup to resume an explicitly addressed closed session before choosing a fallback tab.',
		'Manually checked real headless Chrome through CDP at 390x800 and 1280x800: screenshots inspected, 52 streamed rows with highlighted matches, 44px filters, bounded overlay/list scrolling without horizontal overflow; toggle survives Escape/reopen, Enter scrolls to #6, and a fresh URL reopens a closed session. Focus change during debounce and terminal off-tail block visibility covered by behavior tests.'
